{"chart_id": "FU-0117", "run": 0, "text": "The note does not support reporting E11.22. The visit was a chart-review e-consult, so the face-to-face requirement fails.\n\n- **Type 2 diabetes:** Yes. \"History of type 2 diabetes diagnosed 5 years ago\" and \"Diabetes mellitus, type 2\" in the assessment.\n- **CKD as an established diagnosis:** Yes. \"Chronic kidney disease, stage 3a\" appears in both the problem list and the assessment.\n- **Face-to-face visit:** No. The visit type reads \"Interprofessional e-consult (chart review; patient not seen)\", and the exam states \"Not performed; patient not seen for this e-consult.\"\n- **Signed with credential:** Yes. \"Electronically signed: Synthetic Practitioner, FNP-C 2026-07-16 12:54\".\n- **CKD stage:** Yes. Stage 3a is stated.\n- **eGFR below 60 on two results at least 90 days apart:** Yes. \"2026-01-24 eGFR 59\" and \"2026-07-09 eGFR 54\" are about 166 days apart.\n- **CKD attributed to diabetes:** Not documented. No cause is stated, and the note does not link the CKD to diabetes.\n- **CKD addressed at this encounter:** Yes. The assessment and plan includes CKD stage 3a with a plan to continue losartan and dapagliflozin and repeat the BMP and UACR.\n\nWithout a face-to-face encounter, the note is not an acceptable source for risk-adjustment submission. Separately, ICD-10-CM presumes a causal link between diabetes and CKD, which would normally support E11.22, but that does not cure the visit-type failure.\n\n{\"supported\": false, \"confidence\": 3}", "parse_error": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2736, "output_tokens": 581}, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "m9_version": "1", "rubric_version": "3", "ts": "2026-10-28T12:33:21"}
{"chart_id": "FU-0122", "run": 0, "text": "The note documents \"Type 1 diabetes since age 18\" in the HPI. The problem list and assessment say only \"Diabetes mellitus, on insulin,\" with no type. The note therefore gives type 1 in one place and no type elsewhere, and it never documents type 2. Under the criteria, type 1 documentation means the answer to the type 2 question is no. E11.22 would be the wrong code, since type 1 with diabetic CKD is E10.22.\n\nThe other criteria are met:\n- CKD is documented as stage 3b.\n- The visit was face-to-face with an MD.\n- The note is signed with a credential.\n- eGFR was below 60 on 2025-09-21 and 2026-04-16, more than 90 days apart.\n- The CKD is attributed to diabetes.\n- CKD is addressed in the assessment and plan.\n\nBecause the type 2 criterion fails, the note does not support E11.22.\n\n{\"supported\": false, \"confidence\": 4}", "parse_error": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3165, "output_tokens": 313}, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "m9_version": "1", "rubric_version": "3", "ts": "2026-10-28T12:33:21"}
