{"chart_id": "FU-0282", "run": 0, "text": "The key question is whether the note supports E11.22, which requires T2DM, CKD, and a link between them.\n\n- **T2DM:** Documented as a current diagnosis (\"Diabetes mellitus, type 2\" in the plan).\n- **CKD:** Established as \"CKD 3b, stable on lisinopril\" in the assessment and plan.\n- **Face-to-face visit:** \"Office visit, established patient, face-to-face\" with an FNP-C.\n- **Signature:** \"Electronically signed: Synthetic Practitioner, FNP-C\".\n- **Stage:** 3b is stated.\n- **eGFR:** 32 on 2026-05-09 and 37 on 2026-09-15 are both below 60, but only about 129 days apart, which is at least 90 days.\n- **Attribution to diabetes:** Not stated. The provider never says the CKD is due to diabetes, and the note does not use \"diabetic kidney disease\". Hypertension is also present, and the note does not name a cause.\n- **CKD addressed:** Yes, in plan item 6.\n\nICD-10-CM presumes a causal link between diabetes and CKD under the \"with\" convention, so E11.22 can be coded without explicit attribution unless the provider documents another cause. Here no other cause is documented. Hypertension with CKD would code to I12, and E11.22 would still be reported together with it. The note supports E11.22 on this basis.\n\nThe remaining uncertainty is that the provider did not explicitly link the conditions, which some auditors may want to see.\n\n```json\n{\"supported\": true, \"confidence\": 85}\n```", "parse_error": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3306, "output_tokens": 524}, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "m9_version": "1", "rubric_version": "3", "ts": "2026-10-28T12:33:38"}
